A076,A076.pdf,10.1007/s10209-026-01315-w,12,"ethical artificial intelligence governance in the university digital transformation. In: Vendrell Vidal, E., Cukierman, U.R., Auer, M.E. (eds.) Advanced Technologies and the University of the Future, pp. 201–220. Springer Nature Switzerland, Cham (2025). ​h​t​t​p​s​:​/​/​d​o​i​.​o​r​g​/​1​0​.​1​0​0​7​/​9​7​8​-​3​-​0​3​1​-​7​1​5​3​0​-​3​_​1​4 19. Alier, M., Pereira, J., García-Peñalvo, F.J., Casañ, M.J., Cabré, J.: LAMB: an open-source software framework to create artificial intelligence assistants deployed and integrated into learning man­ agement systems. Comput. Stand. Interfaces. 92, 103940 (2025). ​ h​t​t​p​s​:​/​/​d​o​i​.​o​r​g​/​1​0​.​1​0​1​6​/​j​.​c​s​i​.​2​0​2​4​.​1​0​3​9​4​0 20. Ahmed, S., Rahman, M.S., Kaiser, M.S., Hosen, A.S.M.S.: Advancing personalized and inclusive education for students with personalized support) hint at potential intersections between GenAI and inclusive learning design. These exploratory indications are not sufficient to draw conclusions, but they do identify a promising direction for future research on how AI tools may support learners with diverse needs. Overall, the findings should be interpreted with caution due to methodological constraints, including uneven sample sizes and the use of single knowledge-based tasks per sub­ ject. Nonetheless, the study contributes empirical evidence on how students naturally use GenAI across diverse aca­ demic contexts and provides a foundation for further inquiry into",180
A076,A076.pdf,10.1007/s10209-026-01315-w,12,"constraints, including uneven sample sizes and the use of single knowledge-based tasks per sub­ ject. Nonetheless, the study contributes empirical evidence on how students naturally use GenAI across diverse aca­ demic contexts and provides a foundation for further inquiry into how such tools can be meaningfully and responsibly integrated into higher education. Author contributions All authors contributed equally to the concep­ tion, design, analysis, and writing of the manuscript, working in close collaboration throughout the research process. The work was coordi­ nated by M.A.C., who ensured the alignment of tasks, integration of contributions, and overall coherence of the study. Funding Open access funding provided by FEDER European Funds and the Junta de Castilla y León under the Research and Innovation Strategy for Smart Specialization (RIS3) of Castilla y León 2021- 2027. This research received no funding. Data availability No datasets were generated or analysed during the current study. Declarations Competing interests The authors declare no competing interests. Open Access This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, which permits use, sharing, adaptation, distribution and reproduction in",180
