A080,A080.pdf,10.1007/s10639-024-13184-y,39,"Education and Information Technologies (2025) 30:649–692 687 Table 9 Open ended questions Number Question 35 If you were a teacher would you allow students to use ChatGPT during exams? 36 What do you think about using ChatGPT or other AI chatbot in future? 37 Describe the most interesting experience with ChatGPT or other AI chatbot (positive or negative). 38 Try to suggest how you would use ChatGPT or some other AI chatbot in the education. 39 Did you try to use some other AI chatbot similar to ChatGPT? adequate to represent the latent variables outlined in the main text namely, Perceived Ease of Use (PEU), Enjoyment (Enj), Perceived Value (PV), Perceived Usefulness (PU), Willingness to Use (WU) and Behavioral Intention to Use (BI). Similarly, a model was tested with items of Table 10 answered by all students, loading in factors Concern about AI (CAI) and Behavioral Intention to start using (BI1). Table 6 shows the factorization and the factor loadings that represent the correlation between the measured variable and the latent variable. The validity and consistency of the factorization can",180
A080,A080.pdf,10.1007/s10639-024-13184-y,39,"Concern about AI (CAI) and Behavioral Intention to start using (BI1). Table 6 shows the factorization and the factor loadings that represent the correlation between the measured variable and the latent variable. The validity and consistency of the factorization can be assessed through four measures, calculated using the factors loadings’ values: • Cronbach (α) (Tavakol & Dennick, 2011) and composite reliability (CR) (Hair et al., 2019) are two different measures of internal consistency for each factor, i.e., indicates how closely a set of items loading into one factor are related. Values of α and CR above 0.7 and 0.8, respectively, indicate acceptable internal consistency. • Average variance extracted (AVE) (Fornell & Larcker, 1981) assesses convergent validity that is a measure of how well the latent variable accounts for the variance of the associated indicators. Reporting reliability, convergent and discriminant validity with structural equation modeling: A review and best-practice recommen- dations. Values of AVE above 0.5 are considered adequate. • Discriminant validity (Jöreskog et al., 1989) is a sign that the latent variables are in fact measuring different traits. All the",180
A080,A080.pdf,10.1007/s10639-024-13184-y,39,"with structural equation modeling: A review and best-practice recommen- dations. Values of AVE above 0.5 are considered adequate. • Discriminant validity (Jöreskog et al., 1989) is a sign that the latent variables are in fact measuring different traits. All the correlations between factors have to be lower than the square root of the AVE for each factor. Table 10 Intention to use ChatGPT and concern about it Number Question 40 I ﬁnd that using a tool such as ChatGPT would be a good idea to support learning 41 I will start using ChatGPT to support learning and accomplishing my academic assignments 42 I will ask my colleagues about ChatGPT and how they use it 43 I intend to make it a habit using ChatGPT to support learning and perform my academica assignments 44 I will use ChatGPT or other similar chatbots whenever the opportunity presents itself 45 I have a bad feeling about ChatGPT and AI in general 46 In my opinion using ChatGPT or similar chatbots for academic assignements should not be allowed 123",175
