A080,A080.pdf,10.1007/s10639-024-13184-y,41,"viewed as a manifestation of students’ Intention to Start using ChatGPT and similar AI bots, and the other factor reﬂects their concerns about the AI technology. As reﬂected in the values shown in Table 14, this model meets the criteria for internal consistency and validity, as well as discriminant validity since the square root of AVE for each factor is larger than the correlation between the two constructs, −0.388. Not surprisingly the more worried students are the lower their intention to start using ChaGPT. The main limitation of the models is that only two item load in constructs WU and CAI, and few of the factors loadings are below 0.7 (Hair et al., 2019). The factor loadings indicate how much of the variance of each observed variable (the answer to a given item) is explained by the corresponding latent factor. With the factor loading estimates, factor scores that represent the individual’s level of each latent factor were obtained using a regression method (DiStefano et al., 2009). Table 14 Factor loadings and reliability for the second model Factor Item Loading AVE/CR",180
