A099,A099.pdf,10.1186/s41239-025-00547-9,13,"Page 13 of 35 Wang et al. Int J Educ Technol High Educ (2025) 22:59 Table 3 Survey Items for the Factors Factor Item Reference Trust in GenAI 1. I feel that my decision-making process with GenAI is reliable in language learn- ing. Liu et al. (2015) 2. I feel that my strategies used to reach decisions assisted with GenAI are trust- worthy in language learning. 3. I feel that the information security of GenAI is creditable in language learning. 4. I feel that the efficacy to manage GenAI is believable in language learning. 5. Overall, I think that GenAI is trustworthy to me in language learning. Reliance 6. I depend on GenAI for decision-making in language learning. Cheng et al. (2022) 7. I depend on GenAI for new information or resources as my language learning input. 8. I depend on GenAI for feedback or eval- uation on my language learning output. 9. I depend on GenAI for suggestions on my language learning process. Resistance 10. I oppose the change to the new way of learning language with GenAI. Cheng",180
