A099,A099.pdf,10.1186/s41239-025-00547-9,18,"Page 18 of 35 Wang et al. Int J Educ Technol High Educ (2025) 22:59 As shown in Table 5, the Cronbach’s alpha values for the six factors ranged from 0.832 to 0.963, which were all higher than the threshold of 0.7 (Hair et al., 2010), indicating adequate internal reliability. To assess validity, we first computed the standardized fac- tor loading of each item and the CR and AVE values of each factor to examine conver- gent validity. The standardized factor loadings were between 0.712 and 0.915, all higher than the threshold of 0.5 (Hair et al., 2010). As displayed in Table 6, the CR values were between 0.832 and 0.963, all higher than the 0.7 limit (Kline, 2023). The AVE values were between 0.554 and 0.808, all higher than the threshold of 0.5 (Kline, 2023). These results indicated the establishment of convergent validity. As for discriminant validity, Table 6 shows that the square root of the AVE for each factor was larger than the inter-factor correlation coefficients (Hair et al., 2010), thereby suggesting good discriminant validity. The fitness of",180
A099,A099.pdf,10.1186/s41239-025-00547-9,18,"establishment of convergent validity. As for discriminant validity, Table 6 shows that the square root of the AVE for each factor was larger than the inter-factor correlation coefficients (Hair et al., 2010), thereby suggesting good discriminant validity. The fitness of the model was evaluated through computing and checking the model-fit indices, including χ2/df, CFI, IFI, TLI, NFI, SRMR, and RMSEA. It was found that all the seven indices showed adequate values for the model as χ2/df (2.435) < 3, CFI (0.953) > 0.9, IFI (0.953) > 0.9, TLI (0.949) > 0.9, NFI (0.923) > 0.9, SRMR (0.051) < 0.08, and RMSEA (0.046) < 0.08. Therefore, this model has a good fit. Structural model The structural model involves testing the structural relationships of the proposed hypotheses. In the path analysis, standardized regression weights were calculated, revealing the directions and relationships between factors. Relationships among the six factors were examined to test the hypotheses. Table 7 and Fig. 3 present the results of SEM to examine the hypotheses. It was found that all the ten hypotheses were accepted. First, regarding direct effects,",180
A099,A099.pdf,10.1186/s41239-025-00547-9,18,"factors. Relationships among the six factors were examined to test the hypotheses. Table 7 and Fig. 3 present the results of SEM to examine the hypotheses. It was found that all the ten hypotheses were accepted. First, regarding direct effects, trust in GenAI positively influenced behavioral intention to use (H1: β = 0.442, p < 0.001) Table 7 Hypothesis Testing TGAI trust in GenAI, RL reliance, RS resistance, BIU behavioral intention to use, SD self-directed learning, AU actual use, SE standard error, Sig. value significance value Hypothesis Beta value SE Sig. value Hypothesis result Direct effect H1: TGAI → BIU 0.442 0.054 0.000 Accepted H2: TGAI → RL 0.662 0.053 0.000 Accepted H3: TGAI → RS − 0.095 0.079 0.024 Accepted H4: RL → BIU 0.176 0.046 0.002 Accepted H5: RS → BIU − 0.114 0.018 0.002 Accepted H8: BIU → AU 0.149 0.076 0.000 Accepted H9: SD → AU 0.123 0.070 0.006 Accepted Indirect effect H6: TGAI → RL → BIU 0.117 0.044 0.009 Accepted TGAI → RS → BIU 0.011 0.006 0.029 Accepted H7: TGAI → BIU →",180
