A108,A108.pdf,10.3389/feduc.2026.1734621,9,"All direct hypotheses (H1–H6) were statistically supported, indicating that ChatGPT adoption factors signiﬁcantly enhance student empowerment, which in turn improves satisfaction, continuance intention, and sustainable learning outcomes. To enhance transparency and facilitate visual interpretation of the ﬁndings, the graphical output of the ﬁnal structural model generated using SmartPLS 4.0 is presented in Figure 2. The ﬁgure illustrates all statistically signiﬁcant direct relationships with standardized path coefﬁcients (β), the explained variance (R2) for endogenous constructs, and the signiﬁcant moderating effects of inclusivity perception. This visual representation complements the numerical results reported in Tables 8–12 and provides a holistic overview of the validated model. Figure 2 presents the ﬁnal estimated structural model obtained using SmartPLS 4.0. The ﬁgure displays standardized path coefﬁcients (β) for all signiﬁcant relationships, coefﬁcients of determination (R2) for endogenous constructs, and signiﬁcant moderation effects of inclusivity perception. 4.4 Mediation analysis Mediation effects were examined using a bootstrapping procedure with 5,000 resamples. First, the mediating role of student empowerment (SE) in the relationships between perceived usefulness (PU), perceived ease of use (PEOU), and student satisfaction (SS) was examined. As",180
