A111,A111.pdf,10.1007/s10805-025-09643-x,15,"2101 The Impact of AI Guilt on Students’ Use of ChatGPT for Academic… Discussion Interpretation of Findings This study explores disciplinary differences in how AI guilt affects ChatGPT use for crea- tivity- and routine-based tasks among undergraduate university students. AI guilt sig- nificantly reduces ChatGPT use for creativity-based tasks but has no significant effect on routine-based tasks. In pure fields, the relationship is linear, with higher guilt consistently reducing use. In applied fields, the relationship is nonlinear—AI guilt initially lowers usage, but its effect weakens at higher levels. Students in pure fields are more influenced by internal concerns like justification and perceived risk, while those in applied fields are driven by external social pressures to adopt GenAI tools. These findings extend our under- standing of AI guilt by revealing its varied impact across disciplines and task types. In practice, these results can guide the development of discipline-specific interventions and GenAI ethical policies in higher education. This study empirically validates that AI guilt significantly reduces students’ use of Chat- GPT for creativity-based tasks (H1a) while having no significant impact on routine-based",180
A111,A111.pdf,10.1007/s10805-025-09643-x,15,"results can guide the development of discipline-specific interventions and GenAI ethical policies in higher education. This study empirically validates that AI guilt significantly reduces students’ use of Chat- GPT for creativity-based tasks (H1a) while having no significant impact on routine-based tasks (H1b), corroborating Chan’s (2024) qualitative findings in terms of task differences. Table 4 Logistic regression results for creativity-based task engagement across perceived social norm, per- ceived risk, and rationalization tendency Effect Creativity-based task Perceived_social_norm −0.390 (0.419) - - 1.749** (0.768) Perceived_risk - −1.336*** (0.432) - - Rationalization_tendency - - 0.802* (0.437) 2.825*** (0.771) Perceived_social_norm * Rationalization_ten- dency −3.270*** (0.989) AI_knowledge 3.597*** (1.092) 3.471*** (1.121) 3.626*** (1.094) 3.782*** (1.151) Discipline: Engineering (ref: 1) - Discipline 2: Arts and Social Sciences −0.537 (0.498) −0.391 (0.514) −0.545 (0.500) −0.399 (0.529) - Discipline 3: Science −0.968 (0.609) −1.039 (0.631) −1.016* (0.614) −1.161* (0.644) - Discipline 4: Business −0.116 (0.669) −0.495 (0.701) −0.189 (0.670) −0.091 (0.696) Year (ref: 1) -Undergraduate Year 2 0.178 (0.614) −0.044 (0.632) 0.192 (0.622) 0.139 (0.650) -Undergraduate Year 3 0.948 (0.835) 0.977 (0.853) 0.882 (0.836) 1.015 (0.862) -Undergraduate Year 4",180
