A117,A117.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13575-9,19,"Education and Information Technologies (2025) 30:19741–19764 Table 3 Sample description. Frecuencies and percentatges of degree programs Degree Frequency % Mathematics 3 0.4% Medicine 12 1.6% Pedagogy 10 1.4% Psychology 85 11.5% Chemistry 6 0.8% Labor Relations 37 5.0% Social Work 29 3.9% Tourism 17 2.3% Others 22 3.0% Annex 2. Instruments. Use of ChatGPT. Have you used the AI tool ChatGPT? No, never. Yes, the free version. Yes, the paid premium version. Attitudes toward AI integration in education. 1. The university should provide trainings about how to use AI tools like ChatGPT as a teaching and learning tool. 2. Professors should adapt their teaching methods and evaluation systems to the era of AI. 3. If my university offered a free course on the ethical use of AI tools like ChatGPT, I would enrol. 4. I endorse the use of Artificial Intelligence tools like ChatGPT by professors to evaluate students’ work and exams. 5. The use of Artificial Intelligence tools like ChatGPT should be regulated by pub­ lic institutions: government, university, etc. 6. The use of AI tools like ChatGPT for",180
A117,A117.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13575-9,19,"Intelligence tools like ChatGPT by professors to evaluate students’ work and exams. 5. The use of Artificial Intelligence tools like ChatGPT should be regulated by pub­ lic institutions: government, university, etc. 6. The use of AI tools like ChatGPT for academic tasks should be forbidden. Use frequency of ChatGPT. How often do you use the AI tool ChatGPT?…. Once a month. Once a week. Every day. Several times a day. Purpose of using ChatGPT. What do you use the ChatGPT AI tool for? (You can select multiple answers) Translations. Information search. Completion of homework or academic tasks. Generating texts that I ‘copy and paste’. Answering questions related to academic assignments. Summarizing documents. Entertainment. 1 3 19759",116
A117,A117.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13575-9,20,"Education and Information Technologies (2025) 30:19741–19764 Other purposes. Risk-reward appraisal. To what extent do you agree with the following? The benefits of using ChatGPT outweigh any potential risks. Student perceived value of AI. 1. Students must learn how to use generative AI technologies well for their career. 2. I believe generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT can improve my digital competence. 3. I believe generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT can improve my overall academic performance. 4. I think generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT can help me become a better writer. 5. I can ask questions to generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT that I would otherwise not voice out to my professor. 6. Generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT will not judge me, so I feel com­ fortable with it. 7. I think AI technologies such as ChatGPT is a great tool for student support ser­ vices due to anonymity. 8. I believe generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT can help me save time. 9. I believe AI technologies such as ChatGPT can provide me with unique insights",180
A117,A117.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13575-9,20,"is a great tool for student support ser­ vices due to anonymity. 8. I believe generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT can help me save time. 9. I believe AI technologies such as ChatGPT can provide me with unique insights and perspectives that I may not have thought of myself. 10. I think AI technologies such as ChatGPT can provide me with personalized and immediate feedback and suggestions for my assignments. 11. I think AI technologies such as ChatGPT is a great tool as it is available 24/7. Student perceived cost of AI. 1. Using generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT to complete assignments undermines the value of a university education. 2. Generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT will limit my opportunities to inter­ act with others and socialize while completing coursework. 3. Generative AI technologies such as ChatGPT will hinder my development of generic or transferable skills such as teamwork, problem-solving, and leadership skills. 4. I can become over-reliant on generative AI technologies. Funding Open Access funding provided thanks to the CRUE-CSIC agreement with Springer Nature. No funding has",180
