A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,1,"Effects of ChatGPT on students’ academic performance in Pakistan higher education classrooms Muhammad Azeem Ashraf1, Jan Alam2 & Usama Kalim3 The rapid integration of cutting-edge technology is significantly transforming the higher education landscape. ChatGPT’s groundbreaking technology has provided numerous advantages for higher education. This study explored students’ behavioral intentions to utilize ChatGPT as a learning resource in Pakistani universities and its effect on their academic performance. To accomplish this, the study employed a quantitative descriptive approach to examine the impact of various factors on students’ behavioral intentions, actual behavior, and academic performance. Reflective measurement criteria were adhered to in the development of all indicators and constructs. The study utilized the PLS- SEM to examine the relationships between variables. The findings indicate that ChatGPT platforms have been beneficial in enhancing students’ academic performance within the framework of Pakistani higher education. Behavioral intention serves as the driving force behind students’ actual behaviors, with significant influences from habit and hedonic motivation. These findings are encouraging for fostering a positive perception of ChatGPT usage for learning. Keywords Artificial intelligence, ChatGPT, Higher education, TAM model,",180
A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,1,"intention serves as the driving force behind students’ actual behaviors, with significant influences from habit and hedonic motivation. These findings are encouraging for fostering a positive perception of ChatGPT usage for learning. Keywords Artificial intelligence, ChatGPT, Higher education, TAM model, Higher education institutions OpenAI created ChatGPT (Generative Pre-trained Transformer), which is a language model based on the GPT- 3 architecture designed for interpretation and generation. ChatGPT can be used for natural language processing tasks including chatbots, automated assistants, and customer service, allowing it to comprehend and generate text like humans1. According to Cheung et al.2, modern technology must be integrated into dynamic higher education environments to foster creative and productive learning for educators, administrators, and students3. OpenAI’s ChatGPT, an advanced language model, represents a groundbreaking development that can drastically change our views on academic success and student engagement4. Due to technological advancements, the distinctions between human and artificial intelligence are rapidly diminishing5. The introduction of AI-driven chatbots like ChatGPT raises intriguing questions about their transformative effects on learning experiences and academic outcomes as students navigate the challenges of higher education6,7.",180
A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,1,"technological advancements, the distinctions between human and artificial intelligence are rapidly diminishing5. The introduction of AI-driven chatbots like ChatGPT raises intriguing questions about their transformative effects on learning experiences and academic outcomes as students navigate the challenges of higher education6,7. In the past few years, there has been considerable interest in using advanced technology like ChatGPT for learning and teaching in higher education. It has significant potential to transform how teachers engage with students and facilitate learning8. Covering a wide range of subject areas, this technology is used to create interactive classrooms where students receive individualized feedback and support9. ChatGPT enhances communication in online and hybrid learning environments due to its dynamic nature10, functioning as a virtual assistant for students by answering questions, providing materials, and assisting with homework11. These attributes of ChatGPT promote students’ self-directed learning12 and increase their engagement and interaction13. Moreover, it fosters a more personalized teaching approach by addressing each student’s distinctive learning preferences and needs14. It has improved students’ critical thinking and problem-solving abilities, leading to higher-order cognitive skill development13,15. ChatGPT has influenced higher education",180
A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,1,"engagement and interaction13. Moreover, it fosters a more personalized teaching approach by addressing each student’s distinctive learning preferences and needs14. It has improved students’ critical thinking and problem-solving abilities, leading to higher-order cognitive skill development13,15. ChatGPT has influenced higher education teaching and learning styles16, providing prompt support for assessment and administrative tasks11. Careful consideration must be given to issues such as reluctance to change, concerns about job security, and the need for training on integrating ChatGPT into the curriculum17. The incorporation of ChatGPT into university classrooms has significantly changed the educational landscape18. ChatGPT serves as an innovative tool with tremendous potential to improve the educational process and tailor teaching to individual student learning styles19. According to Shihab et al.20, ChatGPT fosters a flexible instructional environment that supports student interaction. Its use makes learning more exploratory and collaborative, helping students develop deeper interests21. 1Research Institute of Education Sciences, Hunan University, Changsha 410082, China. 2Department of Education, University of Wah, Rawalpindi 47010, Pakistan. 3Smart Learning Institute, Beijing Normal University, Beijing 100875, China. email: Janalam.jk@gmail.com OPEN Scientific Reports | (2025) 15:16434 1 |",180
