A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,9,"affects their academic performance. As supported by earlier studies of Song and Song92, Yu65, Zeb, et al.93, and Huallpa79, active utilization of ChatGPT for learning positively affects students’ academic performance and learning engagement. In line, Tayan et al.69 also suggested that active utilization of the AI platform of ChatGPT helps in effective information retrieval, flexible learning techniques, and improved problem-solving, which ultimately reflect positively on their academic achievement. Jacobi73 also stated that interactive conversations between AI and humans enable students to think critically and look for answers to challenging issues, which helps them perform better. Another essential aim of the study was to examine the various variables that can affect students’ intent to use ChatGPT for learning. The results reveal that habit positively and significantly impacts students’ behavioral intention regarding ChatGPT usage. These results align with the study conducted by De Guinea and Markus62, and Butarbutar et al.63, who noted that habit plays a crucial role in determining students’ intention to consistently use a system within the context of technology adoption. Habit, through cognitive and behavioral processes, facilitates habitual interactions",180
A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,9,"De Guinea and Markus62, and Butarbutar et al.63, who noted that habit plays a crucial role in determining students’ intention to consistently use a system within the context of technology adoption. Habit, through cognitive and behavioral processes, facilitates habitual interactions with technology, ultimately influencing students’ intention to use ChatGPT63. Yu65 also noted that students are more inclined to continue using ChatGPT when they regularly integrate it into their learning process. Furthermore, hedonic motivation also positively impacts students’ behavioral intention. The results correlate with the findings of Junior et al.57 and Chang et al.55, which suggested that hedonic motivation shapes students’ attitudes and perceptions of the tool, in turn affecting their behavior. Ma and Huo56 further elaborated that positive hedonic motivation among students is enhanced by ChatGPT’s natural language processing skills, conversational exchanges, and the potential for a customized and enjoyable learning experience. These two variables (habit and hedonic motivation) have been statistically validated through the study’s results as influencing students’ behavioral intention to utilize ChatGPT for academic purposes. While other variables also showed a positive correlation with behavioral intention, their",180
A122,A122.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-92625-1,9,"learning experience. These two variables (habit and hedonic motivation) have been statistically validated through the study’s results as influencing students’ behavioral intention to utilize ChatGPT for academic purposes. While other variables also showed a positive correlation with behavioral intention, their relationships were not statistically significant according to the tests applied study. Conclusion This study examined the factors affecting students’ intentions and their influence on actual behavior when using ChatGPT for university learning. The research also investigated whether students’ intentions and actual usage of ChatGPT positively impacted their academic performance. Behavioral intention serves as the driving force behind students’ actual behaviors, with habit and hedonic motivation identified as the primary factors influencing these intentions. The results indicate that habit and hedonic motivation are significant predictors of students’ intentions in utilizing ChatGPT for learning purposes. Habits, shaped by cognitive and behavioral processes, enable consistent interactions with the technology, ultimately influencing students’ intentions to use Std. β Sample mean (M) Standard deviation (STDEV) t statistics (|O/STDEV|) P values Actual behavior → academic performance 0.558 0.560 0.058 9.571 0.000 Behavioral intention → academic performance",180
