A130,A130.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13337-7,18,"12698 Education and Information Technologies (2025) 30:12681–12707 significantly higher scores than AI-Reliant Code Generators (p = .047); AI-Inde- pendent Coders had significantly higher scores than AI-Reliant Code Generators (p = .003), AI-Reliant Code Generator & Refiners (p = .016) and AI-Collabora- tive Coders (p = .034). For the 2nd session, the Shapiro-Wilk test revealed that the AI-Assisted Code Refiners deviated significantly from normality, W (43) = 0.862, p < .001, while other profiles did not (all p values > 0.20). Since the data size is large (> 30), normality was assumed (Gravetter & Wallnau, 2011). Levene’s test results showed homogeneity of variances across profiles (all p values > 0.15). Accord- ing to one-way ANOVA results, there was a significant difference in post-test scores across the different AI interaction profiles, F (4, 141) = 3.36, p = .012. The effect size was large, η²= 0.87. Post-hoc comparisons using the Tukey HSD test revealed that AI-Assisted Code Refiners had significantly higher scores than AI-Reliant Code Generator & Refiners (p = .010). For the 3rd session, the Shapiro-Wilk test showed no significant deviation",180
A130,A130.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13337-7,18,"was large, η²= 0.87. Post-hoc comparisons using the Tukey HSD test revealed that AI-Assisted Code Refiners had significantly higher scores than AI-Reliant Code Generator & Refiners (p = .010). For the 3rd session, the Shapiro-Wilk test showed no significant deviation from normality across all profiles (all p values > 0.08). Levene’s test indicated homogeneity of variances (all p values > 0.12). Regarding one-way ANOVA results, there was a significant difference in post-test scores across the different AI interaction profiles, F (4, 135) = 2.98, p = .021. The effect size was large, η²= 0.81. However, the Tukey HSD post hoc test did not identify any specific pairs of groups with significant differences. 5 Discussion This study aimed to investigate the impact of previous programming knowledge on students’ AI interaction profiles, the effect of different AI integration inter- ventions on students’ performance, and the association between AI interaction profiles and students’ performance within each intervention. Additionally, how these interventions influenced students’ AI interaction profiles over time was also examined. Table 5 Mean post-test scores for each activity session AI Interaction Profile",180
