DOC_005,E109.D_2025AHP0009.pdf,10.1587/transinf.2025AHP0009,8,"GPT-4-based AI facilitator, exhibited signif- icantly greater engagement compared to the control group. Students in the treatment condition generated an average of 8.73 posts per student, whereas those in the control group averaged 5.31 posts. This diﬀerence was statistically sig- niﬁcant, (p < .01), representing a 64% increase in original posts relative to the control group. These ﬁndings suggest that the presence of the AI facilitator eﬀectively encouraged students to initiate more discussion threads. While the treatment group also produced more replies per student (M = 8.78) compared to the control group (M = 6.72), this diﬀerence did not reach statistical signiﬁcance (p = .11). Similarly, students in the treatment condition wrote more words on average (approximately 225 words) than those in the control group (approximately 164 words), but this diﬀerence was also not statistically signiﬁcant (p > .10). Interestingly, posts authored by students in the control group received signiﬁcantly more peer “likes” (M = 2.58) than those in the treatment group (M = 0.68), with the dif-",168
