DOC_014,fpsyg-17-1728785.pdf,10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1728785,8,"Wang et al. 10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1728785 Frontiers in Psychology 08 frontiersin.org concluded that the aforementioned three-level coding has reached saturation within the framework of qualitative research. 3.3.1.5 Construction of the theoretical model In this study, Visio software was employed to construct a theoreti­ cal model for the four categories, six factors, and sixteen concepts in the three-level coding table of the research on college students’ AI Literacy (as shown in Figure 1). This construction laid the foundation of the theoretical model for the subsequent quantitative data analysis. 3.3.2 Qualitative data analysis: construction of theoretical models On the basis of the theoretical model developed in the qualitative research, this study advances to the quantitative analysis phase. The objective is to examine and refine the path relationships between vari­ ables within the theoretical model by means of large-scale sample data. 3.3.2.1 Questionnaire development and data collection This research designed a survey questionnaire grounded in the theoretical model of college students’ AI Literacy to examine the rela­ tionships among variables. Table 4 shows the testing scales employed in this study. In the questionnaire designed for",180
