DOC_015,fpsyg-17-1758670.pdf,10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1758670,5,"years, and journal names to ensure that multiple records from the same study were accurately removed. Records with inaccessible full texts were also excluded. Subsequently, two rounds of screening were conducted. In the rst stage, titles, abstracts, and keywords were screened to exclude studies that did not address (a) generative AI, (b) higher education, or (c) measurable learning outcomes. In the second stage, 79 full-text articles were assessed for eligibility against three inclusion criteria: (1) the study examined the impact of generative AI on learning outcomes in higher education; (2) it employed an experimental or quasi-experimental design comparing a GenAI group with a non-GenAI control group, including pre-post designs with a control group; and (3) it reported sucient quantitative information, such as means, standard deviations, sample sizes, to compute eect sizes. After the second-stage screening, 36 studies were retained for the meta-analysis, contributing 132 eect sizes from a total of 7,229 participants. 3.3 Coding procedures and results To examine potential sources of heterogeneity, we coded seven study-level moderators. Table 3 presents the coding results for each moderator, whereas Appendix A",180
DOC_015,fpsyg-17-1758670.pdf,10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1758670,5,"the meta-analysis, contributing 132 eect sizes from a total of 7,229 participants. 3.3 Coding procedures and results To examine potential sources of heterogeneity, we coded seven study-level moderators. Table 3 presents the coding results for each moderator, whereas Appendix A reports the full coding results for all 36 studies and 132 eect sizes. The coding process was completed independently by two authors, and the inter-rater reliability was substantial (Cohen’s k D 0.832). Because the moderators diered in the extent to which they required interpretive judgment, their coding procedures are reported with dierent levels of detail below. 3.3.1 Discipline category, measurement tool, and intervention duration These moderators involved relatively low-inference coding because the relevant information was typically reported explicitly in the primary studies. Therefore, these moderators were coded directly based on study characteristics, following groupings commonly adopted in recent syntheses on the eects of educational technology on learning outcomes. The coding results for these moderators are shown in Table 3. 3.3.2 Learning task type Learning task type was coded into two categories: knowledge acquisition and problem resolution, as discussed in the",180
DOC_015,fpsyg-17-1758670.pdf,10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1758670,5,"the eects of educational technology on learning outcomes. The coding results for these moderators are shown in Table 3. 3.3.2 Learning task type Learning task type was coded into two categories: knowledge acquisition and problem resolution, as discussed in the literature review. Coding was based on the primary task reected in the learning activities. Studies were coded as knowledge acquisition when the main task focused on understanding, explaining, summarizing, or applying existing knowledge in relatively well- dened ways. They were coded as problem resolution when the primary task emphasized solving problems, generating solutions, making decisions, or addressing open-ended challenges. When task features overlapped, coding was based on the task type that played the most central role in structuring the learning activities. 3.3.3 Teaching method In addition, teaching method was identied as particularly consequential because existing research suggests that learning eects depend more on pedagogy than on the medium of delivery. As no established external framework provides a denitive classication of GenAI-related teaching methods, we adopted a consistent pedagogy-based coding strategy. Each study was assigned to the single category that most",180
DOC_015,fpsyg-17-1758670.pdf,10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1758670,5,"depend more on pedagogy than on the medium of delivery. As no established external framework provides a denitive classication of GenAI-related teaching methods, we adopted a consistent pedagogy-based coding strategy. Each study was assigned to the single category that most accurately captured the dominant instructional logic reected in its learning activities, rather than the delivery medium. Teaching method was coded according to the dominant pedagogical logic reected in the learning activities. In assigning categories, we considered three aspects in combination: (a) the core learning activity required of students, (b) the role of the Frontiers in Psychology 05 frontiersin.org",98
