DOC_015,fpsyg-17-1758670.pdf,10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1758670,7,"quality To address study quality concerns, this review conducted a methodological quality appraisal of the included studies. Drawing on the core logic of the EPHPP guideline and taking into account the characteristics of educational experimental and quasi- experimental research (Thomas et al., 2004), ve domains were evaluated: (1) research design, (2) baseline equivalence between groups, (3) outcome measurement quality, (4) attrition and data completeness, and (5) intervention implementation and statistical analysis. Each domain was rated as high, medium, or low quality. The overall study quality rating was determined according to the number of domains rated as low: studies with no low-rated domains were classied as high quality; those with one low-rated domain were classied as medium quality; and those with two or more low- rated domains were classied as low quality. Study quality was used only for sensitivity analysis and was not included as a moderator in the moderator analyses. 3.4 Calculation of the e",155
