DOC_022,Leveraging ChatGPT to enhance problem-solving skills and technology acceptance among undergraduates  an exploratory experimental study in Sri Lankan h.pdf,10.1080/2331186X.2026.2703353,12,"(1989) and Scherer et al. (2019). Perceived Usefulness (three items: ‘ChatGPT would be useful’, ‘improve my productivity’, ‘help me learn new concepts’): M ¼ 3.49, SD ¼ 0.81, a ¼ 0.82. Behavioural Intention to Use (two items: ‘intend to continue using’, ‘would recommend to others’): M ¼ 3.34, SD ¼ 1.08, a ¼ 0.83. Both constructs exceeded the accepted reliability threshold of a  0.70 (Nunnally, 1978). Perceived ease of use was measured with single items per group (control group: M ¼ 3.73, SD ¼ 0.80; experimental group: M ¼ 3.54, SD ¼ 0.96); as items were administered to separate groups, inter-item reliability could not be computed and this construct is reported descriptively only. Table 4. Descriptive statistics for experimental group. N Minimum Maximum Mean Std. deviation Variance Statistic Statistic Statistic Statistic Statistic Statistic Problem understanding 37 12.00 23.00 17.78 2.85 8.12 Strategic thinking 37 10.00 21.00 15.84 2.70 7.31 Solution quality 37 14.00 23.00 18.24 2.31 5.36 Implementation planning 37 5.00 15.00 9.89 2.59 6.71 Communication 37 3.00 7.00 5.16 1.26 1.58 Total points 37 44.00 89.00 66.92 11.38",180
