DOC_024,NEW03.pdf,10.1016/j.caeai.2025.100385,14,"with brainstorming schoolwork ideas, helping structure writing assignments, and assisting with translation or language learning, elicit more discrepancies in opinions among students with different SES; this attitudinal divergence is even more clearly manifested for all displacement activities. Consequently, some support activities tend to be less controversial than others, such as requesting personalized feedback on assignments and creating study plans and schedules. Correspondingly, educators can grasp a better understanding of this emerging consensus and direct more attention towards contentious activities to explore the underlying reasoning of sociodemographic discrepancies in acceptance. Table B.1 Significant Regression Coefficients of SES and Demographics with Each Activity Acceptability, Phase 2 Activity Significant Coefficients Academic Support #1 Improve your understanding of course concepts or problems ns #2 Assist with brainstorming schoolwork ideas Student SES (β = -.07, p = .02) Family SES (β = .08, p = .007) Gender (Female) (β = .06, p = .04) #3 Proofread and improve writing assignments upon completion Student SES (β = -.07, p = .02) #4 Conduct some initial information searches for schoolwork ns #5 Help structure writing assignments Student",180
