DOC_029,NEW09.pdf,10.1016/j.ssaho.2025.101886,6,"as a synthesis of both approaches, emerges as a comprehensive strategy, combining the iterative refinement of the in­ sights of both process and genre approaches. This harmonization rec­ ognizes writing precision as a multifaceted skill, addressing both the dynamic evolution of the writing process and the nuanced demands of genre-specific language use. The eclectic framework, by integrating these strengths, provides students with a holistic framework for navi­ gating the intricate interplay of language and genre, offering a potent methodology to nurture their mastery of writing precision. As exem­ plified by participant (P) 7: “The pedagogy provided me a strategy for enhancing writing precision by seamlessly integrating both writing approaches.”-P7 The same results were found at researcher’s fieldnote #1 as follows: “Students improved their command of writing by working on mul­ tiple drafts and revisions, collaborating effectively to enhance each other’s accuracy. They applied genre-specific language features, demonstrating a stronger grasp of writing in various contexts.” 4.2.1.2. Refined overall language proficiency. The eclectic writing peda­ gogy serves as a key instrument in improving students’ writing skills by fostering a substantial comprehension",180
DOC_029,NEW09.pdf,10.1016/j.ssaho.2025.101886,6,"accuracy. They applied genre-specific language features, demonstrating a stronger grasp of writing in various contexts.” 4.2.1.2. Refined overall language proficiency. The eclectic writing peda­ gogy serves as a key instrument in improving students’ writing skills by fostering a substantial comprehension pertaining to linguistic elements, vocabulary, and the distinct functions of various genres. Through this framework, participants gain advanced proficiency in grammar, syntax, rhetoric, and genre-specific details, leading to a more precise use of language. P4 highlighted the framework’s positive impact on writing abilities, encouraging experimentation with various writing techniques. Table 2 Students’ writing task performance (Descriptive Genre). Writing Aspects Task#1 Task#2 Task#3 Task#4 Mean SD Mean SD Mean SD Mean SD Task Response 16.05 1.40 17.05 1.44 16.45 1.49 16.21 1.67 Coherence-cohesion 16.20 1.69 17.01 1.51 16.40 1.41 16.05 1.54 Grammatical & Structural Accuracy 16.10 1.29 14.20 1.76 14.20 1.69 16.01 1.89 Lexical Resource 15.30 1.67 16.90 1.59 16.00 1.52 14.23 1.72 Logical Order 16.00 1.60 16.10 1.61 16.15 1.73 15.17 1.39 Overall 15.93 1.67 16.25 1.79 15.82 1.74 15.53 1.56 R.J. Robillos Social Sciences & Humanities Open 12 (2025)",180
