DOC_029,NEW09.pdf,10.1016/j.ssaho.2025.101886,7,"“The eclectic approach exposed me to various genres and had the op­ portunity to experiment with writing techniques and elements.” -P4 4.2.2. Affordances of GPT-based chatbots in facilitating students’ writing tasks (theme 2) 4.2.2.1. Writing practice. Interacting with chatbots gives learners reg­ ular practice in composing questions, responses, and full sentences in the target language. This consistent engagement improves fluency and ac­ curacy while encouraging critical thinking in vocabulary use, grammar, and structure. Observing chatbot responses also helps learners inter­ nalize patterns and apply them effectively to their own writing, as P1 shared: “The more I practice writing, the more I refine my skills especially in punctuation, coherence, and structure.” -P1 Fieldnote #2 below was found to be in parallel with interview results above: “Students showed critical thinking by creating coherent questions and responses, improving vocabulary, sentence structure, and grammar. Regular practice enhanced their ability to write complex sentences, and they learned by modeling chatbot patterns, which boosted fluency and idea expression.” 4.2.2.2. Immediate feedback. ChatGPT provides immediate feedback on learners’ language accuracy and clarity by highlighting and correcting errors",180
DOC_029,NEW09.pdf,10.1016/j.ssaho.2025.101886,7,"Regular practice enhanced their ability to write complex sentences, and they learned by modeling chatbot patterns, which boosted fluency and idea expression.” 4.2.2.2. Immediate feedback. ChatGPT provides immediate feedback on learners’ language accuracy and clarity by highlighting and correcting errors in grammar, phrasing, and vocabulary. For example, if a learner writes, ‘I uses a social media,’ the AI responds with the correct form, ‘I use a social media,’ helping learners internalize proper grammar and sen­ tence structure. One participant (P5) shared: “ChatGPT helped me improve my language skills accurately by providing me immediate feedback on the errors I committed on my text.” -P5 4.2.2.3. Reduced anxiety. Using a GPT-based chatbots offers a low- pressure language practice setting. Unlike interactions with native speakers, there is no immediate social judgment or pressure for perfec­ tion. Learners can freely explore, learn, and make mistakes without anxiety. This allows them to focus on improvement instead of worrying about errors. As learners practice and realize effective communication with Ai, their language confidence increases. P4 expressed: “I don’t feel any pressure of a live conversation in",180
DOC_029,NEW09.pdf,10.1016/j.ssaho.2025.101886,7,"mistakes without anxiety. This allows them to focus on improvement instead of worrying about errors. As learners practice and realize effective communication with Ai, their language confidence increases. P4 expressed: “I don’t feel any pressure of a live conversation in using ChatGPT. I can play with vocabulary and explore creative language use.”-P4 Fieldnote #3 was found to align with the interview results above: “ChatGPT reduced anxiety by letting students explore and make mistakes without judgment, creating a low-pressure environment that boosted confidence, encouraged practice, and supported effec­ tive communication.” 4.2.3. Merits of ChatGPT in eclectic writing pedagogy for genre writing (theme 3) 4.2.3.1. Tailored learning experience. The intervention personalizes genre-based writing by adapting to diverse learning styles and needs. Table 3 Students’ writing task performance (Narrative Genre). Writing Aspects Task#1 Task#2 Task#3 Task#4 Mean SD Mean SD Mean SD Mean SD Task Response 16.00 1.34 16.99 1.32 17.18 1.11 17.31 1.33 Coherence-cohesion 15.91 1.23 16.34 1.17 16.40 1.23 16.99 1.35 Grammatical & Structural Accuracy 16.56 1.13 15.76 1.65 15.25 1.51 16.89 1.18 Lexical Resource 15.34 1.67 16.18 1.95 16.28 1.25",180
