DOC_031,NEW13.pdf,10.1007/s44217-026-02329-5,7,"Page 7 of 16 Babaee Discover Education (2026) 5:1211 conditions. Coding was interpretive rather than reliability-oriented; therefore, an inter- coder agreement coefficient was not used as a quality criterion. Quotations were selected to illustrate both positive and cautionary accounts. The qualitative findings were used to contextualize possible revision processes without being treated as direct evidence that a particular mechanism caused the quantitative outcomes. 4 Results 4.1 Writing outcome differences across feedback conditions Descriptive patterns are presented in Table 2; Fig. 1. The ChatGPT condition began with somewhat higher means on task achievement, coherence and cohesion, lexical resource, and overall writing, whereas grammatical accuracy was similar. None of the base­ line differences was statistically significant: task achievement, Welch t = 0.88, p = .382; Table 2 Descriptive statistics for writing outcomes by feedback condition Outcome Time ChatGPT M ChatGPT SD Teacher M Teacher SD Mean difference Task achievement Pretest 4.36 1.47 3.95 1.63 0.41 Task achievement Posttest 5.48 1.45 4.29 1.23 1.19 Task achievement Gain 1.12 1.42 0.33 1.85 0.79 Coherence and cohesion Pretest 4.24 1.27 3.81 1.44 0.43 Coherence and",180
