DOC_036,NEW19.pdf,10.1186/s41239-026-00619-4,21,"test along the X-axis (SVD1) showed significant dif­ ferences across all window sizes, including windows three, four, six, and seven. At a win­ dow size of three lines Learning Analytics (Mdn = − 0.16, N = 21) was statistically signifi­ cantly different at the alpha = 0.05 level from Artificial Intelligence (Mdn = 0.26, N = 18 U = 375.00, p < 0.001, r = − 0.98). This difference remained significant at window sizes of 4 lines (Mdn = 0.29, N = 18 U = 373.00, p < 0.001, r = − 0.97), 6 lines (Mdn = 0.32, N = 18 U = 368.00, p < 0.001, r = − 0.95) and 7 lines (Mdn = 0.32, N = 18 U = 368.00, p < 0.001, r = − 0.95). These findings are similar to the significant difference found in the selected 5-window stanza. In contrast, no significant difference was found along the X-axis (SVD2) at any window size. At a window size of three lines the Mann–Whitney test showed that Learning Ana­ lytics (Mdn = 0.11, N = 21)",180
