DOC_036,NEW19.pdf,10.1186/s41239-026-00619-4,21,"window sizes revealed a dimension-specific robustness in relation to the window stanza from 3 to 7 lines. Testing of different weighted models To test the robustness of the network structure produced by the primary ENA model, three alternative weighting transformations, Square Root, Natural Log, and Product, were applied to the same dataset and compared with the binary model selected as the baseline for this analysis. Across all four models, the underlying network structure was consistent. CTX, CPS, ASSESS, D.SDT and TECH defining the Artificial Intelligence (blue, on the right) side and CTX, ACT, COURSE, and SUPP defining the Learning Analytics (red, on the left) side. Figure 1 displays the comparison plot using the binary model. Figures 2, 3 and 4 are weighted models. Abbreviations LD Learning design ENA Epistemic network analysis GenAI Generative artificial intelligence HCLA Human-centred learning analytics LA Learning analytics OULDI Open university learning design initiative QE Quantitative ethnography SDT Self-determination theory SVD Singular value decomposition Acknowledgements The authors express gratitude to all the participants for their involvement and cooperation in this study.",175
