DOC_038,NEW22.pdf,10.3389/feduc.2026.1833616,16,"Facilitating conditions signiﬁcantly and positively affected perceived ease of use (β=0.150, t = 3.378, p = 0.001), supporting H3a, but had no signiﬁcant effect on perceived usefulness (β=0.052, p = 0.239), rejecting H3b. Perceived intelligence signiﬁcantly and positively inﬂuenced perceived usefulness (β=0.128, t = 2.869, p = 0.004), supporting H4b, but had no signiﬁcant effect on perceived ease of use (β=0.007, p = 0.890), rejecting H4a. Both subjective norms (β=0.463, t = 10.964, p < 0.001) and perceived behavioral control (β=0.299, t = 7.024, p < 0.001) signiﬁcantly and positively affected attitude, supporting H5 and H6. Perceived usefulness (β=0.406, t = 7.158, p < 0.001) and attitude (β=0.289, t = 5.321, p < 0.001) signiﬁcantly and positively inﬂuenced adoption intention, supporting H8 and H9, while perceived ease of use had no signiﬁcant effect on adoption intention (β=0.060, p = 0.157), rejecting H7. 5.3 Mediation effect analysis Based on path analysis results of the structural model, this study systematically examined the mediating effects of perceived usefulness, perceived ease of use, and attitude using 5,000 bias- FIGURE 2 The measurement model. TABLE",180
