DOC_039,NEW23.pdf,10.1016/j.chbah.2026.100327,7,"prior to analysis. First, a model was examined with AI-based lower-order cognitive offloading as the dependent variable and the perceived value of AI as the independent variable. The results are presented in Tables 4 and 5. The tables report standardized regression coefficients and R2 values, which help indicate the magnitude of the observed associations. The perceived value of AI is positively associated with AI-based lower-order cognitive offloading (  = 0.08; p < 0.001). The perceived value of AI is also positively associated with the AI-usage capability, and the AI-usage capability is positively associated with AI-based lower-order cognitive offloading. In addition, the interaction term between the AI evaluation capability and AI-usage capability is positively associated with AI-based lower-order cognitive offloading. Further conditional indirect effect analysis showed that when the AI evaluation capability was low (−1 SD), the indirect effect of the perceived value of AI on AI-based lower-order offloading through the AI- usage capability was 0.42, with a bootstrapped 95% CI [0.22, 0.66], which did not include zero, indicating a significant mediation effect. When the AI evaluation capability was high",180
