DOC_040,NEW24.pdf,10.3389/feduc.2026.1892057,8,"The Cronbach’s alpha and composite reliability (rho_c) values exceeded the recommended threshold of 0.70 for all constructs, confirming the adequate internal reliability of the scales used (Hair et al., 2021). Likewise, the rho_A coefficients reached values above 0.70, reinforcing the stability and consistency of the indicators associated with each latent variable. On the other hand, convergent validity was corroborated using AVE, yielding values above the minimum criterion of 0.50 established by Fornell and Larcker (1981), indicating that the constructs satisfactorily explain the variance of their indicators. Therefore, the results presented in Table 4 show that the measurement model exhibits adequate levels of psychometric quality, supporting the reliability and validity of the constructs used to analyze the use of GenAI tools among marketing university students. The values obtained using the HTMT criterion remained below the critical threshold of 0.85 recommended by Henseler et al. (2015), indicating that the dimensions assessed do not exhibit conceptual overlap (Table 5). This demonstrates that the constructs represent distinct phenomena in the analysis of GenAI tool use. Consequently, the model’s conceptual structure maintains theoretical consistency and",180
DOC_040,NEW24.pdf,10.3389/feduc.2026.1892057,8,"Henseler et al. (2015), indicating that the dimensions assessed do not exhibit conceptual overlap (Table 5). This demonstrates that the constructs represent distinct phenomena in the analysis of GenAI tool use. Consequently, the model’s conceptual structure maintains theoretical consistency and discriminant validity, strengthening the methodological robustness of the instrument and the stability of the structural relationships proposed in the study. 4.2 Evaluation of the structural model All VIF values remained within the acceptable limits recommended for PLS-SEM studies, indicating the absence of multicollinearity issues among the predictor constructs. The highest value corresponded to the relationship between hedonic motivation and behavioral intention (VIF = 3.391); however, this result remains methodologically acceptable as it falls below the maximum threshold of 5 suggested by Hair et al. (2021). Likewise, although Becker et al. (2015) propose a more conservative criterion of 3.3 to identify potential multicollinearity issues, the obtained value does not pose a problem for the model’s stability, especially considering that the constructs involved correspond to theoretically distinct dimensions within the UTAUT2 model. Table 6. According to Falk and Miller (1992), a structural",180
DOC_040,NEW24.pdf,10.3389/feduc.2026.1892057,8,"potential multicollinearity issues, the obtained value does not pose a problem for the model’s stability, especially considering that the constructs involved correspond to theoretically distinct dimensions within the UTAUT2 model. Table 6. According to Falk and Miller (1992), a structural model has acceptable explanatory power when the R2 values of the endogenous constructs exceed the minimum threshold of 0.10, a criterion indicating that the predictor variables are sufficiently relevant to explain the variance in the dependent construct. In this study, the R2 and adjusted R2 values obtained for behavioral intention to use (BI) and use of GenAI tools (UI) far exceeded this criterion, demonstrating the high predictive power of the proposed model (Table 7). In particular, the UI construct achieved an R2 of 0.707, indicating that 70.7% of the variance in TABLE 3 Continued Indicators BI EE FC HM HT PE PV SI UI SI4 0.748 SI5 0.715 SI6 0.742 UI1 0.893 UI2 0.864 UI3 0.829 UI4 0.784 UI5 0.907 UI6 0.828 Items EE4, EE5, FC3, and SI7 were removed because they did not meet the minimum criterion for external",180
