DOC_040,NEW24.pdf,10.3389/feduc.2026.1892057,11,"obtained by the linear model (LM), demonstrating adequate predictive performance of the UTAUT2 model in the context of GenAI tool use by marketing students. 4.4 Importance-performance map analysis The IPMA analysis applied to the UTAUT2 model allowed for the simultaneous evaluation of the overall importance of the constructs and their level of performance regarding the use of GenAI tools (Figure 2). The results show that habit (HT) reported the highest level of total importance within the model, while also achieving moderate performance, confirming its strategic relevance in explaining the use of GenAI tools. Likewise, behavioral intention to use (BI) exhibited high total importance, although with lower performance levels compared to other constructs in the model. On the other hand, constructs such as hedonic motivation (HM), effort expectancy (EE), and performance expectancy (PE) showed relatively high levels of performance, although with TABLE 11 Evaluation of the model’s predictive capacity using PLSpredict . Constructs Q2predict PLS-SEM_RMSE PLS-SEM_MAE LM_RMSE LM_MAE IA_RMSE IA_MAE BU1 0.601 0.639 0.456 0.638 0.469 1.011 0.830 BU2 0.531 0.736 0.542 0.796 0.592 1.075 0.894 BU3 0.452 0.753 0.512 0.769",180
