DOC_043,s10639-025-13533-5.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13533-5,8,"Education and Information Technologies (2025) 30:19111–19140 and iterated to ensure the relevance and clarity of the questions prior to the formal data collection. 2.3 Sampling and participants Probability sampling was used to recruit respondents across IT-focused educational programs within the Technical Faculty of IT and Design. The target population consists of 1st and 5th semester students studying Interaction Design, Information Technology, Medialogy, Artificial Intelligence Engineering, Techno-Anthropology, Computer Engineering, Robotics, and Sustainable Design. This sampling includes students at different stages of their academic journey, and thus with different levels of familiarity with studying in a PBL environment. The rationale for choosing this target population is grounded in their academic discipline and the relevance of GenAI within their field of study, and it is assumed that it will ensure a sufficient level of interest, expertise, and familiarity with GenAI. The survey was designed and administered using SurveyXact. An invitation email containing a survey link was sent to all 1st and 5th semester students. The survey remained open for approximately one month during the winter of 2023. A total of 119 responses were",180
DOC_043,s10639-025-13533-5.pdf,10.1007/s10639-025-13533-5,8,"designed and administered using SurveyXact. An invitation email containing a survey link was sent to all 1st and 5th semester students. The survey remained open for approximately one month during the winter of 2023. A total of 119 responses were collected, out of which 36 responses were excluded due to incompleteness, resulting in a final sample of 83 responses. The distribution of respondents by academic semester indicated a higher response rate among 1st semester students (63%) compared to 5th semester students (37%), which reflects the larger size of the 1st semester cohorts. Respondents ranged in age from 19 to 31 Item N % Semester 1st semester 52 63% 5th semester 31 37% Age 19–20 13 16% 21–22 37 45% 23–24 20 24% 25+ 13 16% Gender Female 19 23% Male 61 73% Non-binary 1 1% Other 1 1% Prefer not to say 1 1% Field of study Artificial Intelligence Engineering 6 7% Computer Engineering 5 6% Cyber– and computer technology 10 12% Information Technology 3 4% Interaction Design 4 5% Medialogy 15 18% Robotics 19 23% Software 4 5% Sustainable",180
