DOC_047,s10639-026-14100-2.pdf,10.1007/s10639-026-14100-2,26,"1 3 8728 Education and Information Technologies (2026) 31:8703–8730 Declarations Competing interests This study was performed on the authors’ own incentive, inspired by the paradigm shift caused by Generative AI and its potential, but yet not fully explored, impact on higher education and society at large. The work is implicitly supported by the authors’ universities, which provided time and resources to conduct the study and distribute the questionnaire. However, the study otherwise lacks finan­ cial incentives, such as external grants or funding, nor was the study requested by any governing body at any of the authors’ universities. Instead, the driving force behind the study is our own curiosity, which is why the study aims to explore how students use and perceive Generative AI in their education. The goal is to acquire insights and understanding that could, potentially, be favorable as a baseline for future studies and decision support of how to adapt education at the studied universities. Authors’ related studies in the last 3 years on the topic have similar goals, but take a neutral, exploratory stance towards Generative AI",180
