DOC_051,s11528-026-01191-4.pdf,10.1007/s11528-026-01191-4,5,"785 TechTrends (2026) 70:781–795 Text‑to‑Image/Image‑to‑Image Image generative AI tools provide participants with still images (see left image in Fig. 2) when prompted with text (text-to-image generation). Additionally, text-to-image GenAI tools also produce images when participants use reference images with the prompts. Image prompts occur when participants input another authentic image, generative image, or an image copied from the Internet into the GenAI tool, along with text, to improve a text-to-image output. The AI-driven course includes some of these tools for instruc- tional training: Midjourney (version 6 model), Leonardo AI (version 2 model), LLMs (ChatGPT), and more. Text‑to‑Video/Image‑to‑Video Generative AI tools that provide video outputs when prompted with text (text-to-video. generation) or image (image-to-video generation) include Luma Labs, RunwayML (Gen 3 model), and more. (see Table 2). Participants use these GenAI tools to support independent and group coursework that requires video com- ponents. Figure 3 shows still shots from a video created by students using text prompts and image prompts, who used several text-to-video and image generators to produce vari- ous video scenes for a brand campaign advertisement. Text‑to‑Audio/Speech Participants also",180
DOC_051,s11528-026-01191-4.pdf,10.1007/s11528-026-01191-4,5,"com- ponents. Figure 3 shows still shots from a video created by students using text prompts and image prompts, who used several text-to-video and image generators to produce vari- ous video scenes for a brand campaign advertisement. Text‑to‑Audio/Speech Participants also work with text-to-audio generative tools such as ElevenLabs (see Fig. 4), where text is used to pro- duce audio in the form of conversation and narrative gen- erative voices/speeches. For example, participants enter the script of the conversation, select voice type from samples provided, and the model then generates a speech/conversa- tional audio (see Fig. 4). AI Video Enhancement Tools Participants work with digital editing tools that host AI fea- tures. For instance, Adobe Premiere Pro is software that has AI features that provide users with video editing capabilities. Fig. 2 An example of Text- To-Image/Image-To-Image. Note. The image on the left is generated by Midjourney via a text prompt. The image on the right is a still shot of a video generated by Hedra. The left image was input as a prompt into Hedra, which generated a speaking virtual",180
