DOC_051,s11528-026-01191-4.pdf,10.1007/s11528-026-01191-4,6,"786 TechTrends (2026) 70:781–795 Most participants utilized this product for editing brand cam- paign videos. Coursework Activities Students engaged in diverse assignments (see Table 3). For instance, students worked in pairs and engaged in the fol- lowing steps to create a business/brand campaign video: (1) researching and testing ideas for brand and demographic campaign opportunities, and scripting; (2) generating images; (3) utilizing video generators using text and image prompts; (4) editing generated videos in Adobe Premiere Pro; and (5) adding voice-over and music to complete the video advertisement. In this assignment example, students critically analyzed the messages and communication styles produced, as well as how GenAI tools and LLMs can be manipulated to support and generate such outputs. Research Procedures The research was approved by the Institutional Review Board (IRB) on the campus where the study was con- ducted. At the start of the Fall semester, students were introduced to the study by the leading author. By the end of January in 2025, five participants eagerly agreed to be interviewed via Zoom. After each student consented to the form, an",180
DOC_051,s11528-026-01191-4.pdf,10.1007/s11528-026-01191-4,6,"the start of the Fall semester, students were introduced to the study by the leading author. By the end of January in 2025, five participants eagerly agreed to be interviewed via Zoom. After each student consented to the form, an individual interview was conducted and recorded. Upon completion of the interview, the transcript generated by Zoom was reviewed. The first author, who conducted all interviews, carefully read each transcript and corrected minor errors. The finalized transcripts were then sent to the interviewees for verification. All participants confirmed the accuracy of their transcripts. Fig. 4 An example of Text-to-Audio/Speech in ElevenLabs. Note. The above is a student’s text input in ElevenLabs. The student’s prompt led to a generated speech that spoke the student’s input Table 3 AI-Driven Course Activities Activity Type Instructions Explore LLM Individual Record two events on campus. Synthesize, find themes and create new content from event information. Record and transcribe them using a LLM or any GenAI tools. Create a virtual influencer Individual Use GenAI tools to research a specific content area to create a virtual influencer. Create:",180
DOC_051,s11528-026-01191-4.pdf,10.1007/s11528-026-01191-4,6,"find themes and create new content from event information. Record and transcribe them using a LLM or any GenAI tools. Create a virtual influencer Individual Use GenAI tools to research a specific content area to create a virtual influencer. Create: persona docu- mentation, image models (more than five images of the same created image). Present an AI tool Individual Present an AI tool/platform not learned in class, include pros and cons, practical uses of the tool. Make a political ad Group Work in pairs to produce a 30-second political advertisement for or against an electoral candidate. Multimedia video project Group Pairs create a compelling brand specific deliverables using various generative tools. Include video, audio, and still images. Research AI Policies Individual Conduct research, analyzing AI policies for media companies in your field, and use what you learn to write your own AI policy for a media company you intend to work for one day. Create a business campaign Group In teams of two, create a 360° media campaign for an assigned company using the tools we explore throughout the course.",180
