DOC_055,s41239-026-00579-9.pdf,10.1186/s41239-026-00579-9,23,"this debate is the need to pro­ vide the necessary infrastructure and education for the proper use of AI. Simply banning these tools, instead of addressing the root causes of potential problems, is not a long-term solution. Instead of prohibition, efforts should focus on developing strategies that promote responsible and ethical use of AI in education. This includes educating both teachers and students on how to effectively utilize AI, creating clear guidelines to prevent misuse, and designing learning activities that foster critical thinking even in the presence of AI. Only in this way can we harness the potential of AI to personal­ ize education, assist teachers, and prepare students for a future in which AI will play a significant role 1The original essay was in Persian and has been translated into English for presentation in this article Table 5 (continued)",140
