DOC_059,s41598-025-32692-6.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-32692-6,8,"To assess discriminant validity, both the Fornell–Larcker criterion and the HTMT ratio were applied. As shown in Table 4, the square roots of AVE for TTF (0.821), PU (0.833), and RGU (0.829) were greater than the corresponding inter-construct correlations, satisfying the Fornell–Larcker criterion. Similarly, Table 5 reports the HTMT values, which ranged from 0.363 to 0.415. All values were well below the conservative threshold of 0.85, further confirming discriminant validity. Taken together, these results demonstrate that the measurement model has strong reliability, convergent validity, and discriminant validity, providing a solid foundation for subsequent structural model analysis. Construct1 Construct2 HTMT TTF PU 0.363 TTF RGU 0.415 PU RGU 0.382 Table 5. HTMT results. TTF PU RGU TTF 0.821 0.314 0.373 PU 0.314 0.833 0.340 RGU 0.373 0.340 0.829 Table 4. Fornell–Larcker criterion. Construct Cronbach’s α CR AVE TTF 0.879 0.912 0.674 PU 0.853 0.901 0.694 RGU 0.909 0.929 0.687 Table 3. Reliability results for TTF, PU, and RGU. Fig. 2. Distribution of TTF, PU, and RGU Scale Means (Boxplots; Likert 1–5, n = 280). Scientific Reports | (2026) 16:2759 8 |",180
