DOC_059,s41598-025-32692-6.pdf,10.1038/s41598-025-32692-6,9,"Structural model analysis The measurement and structural models were estimated using ML with FIML (n = 280). The three-factor measurement model exhibited excellent global fit (Table 6): χ²(87) = 94.598, χ²/df = 1.087, CFI = 0.997, TLI = 0.996, RMSEA = 0.018 with 90% CI [0.000, 0.038], and SRMR = 0.027. The standardized factor structure and the hypothesized structural relations are visualized in Fig. 3, which also presents the standardized path estimates for interpretation alongside the fit indices in Table 6. In the structural model, all hypothesized paths were positive and statistically significant (Table 7; see also Fig. 3). Task–Technology Fit (TTF) was positively associated with Perceived Usefulness (PU; β = 0.360, p < .001), and both TTF (β = 0.318, p < .001) and PU (β = 0.273, p < .001) were positively related to Responsible GenAI Use (RGU). These results indicate that closer alignment between GenAI tools and academic tasks is associated with higher perceived usefulness and, in turn, with more responsible use behaviors, while a direct path from TTF to RGU remains (Table 7; Fig. 3). Bootstrapped",180
