DOC_060,s41598-026-54337-y_reference.pdf,10.1038/s41598-026-54337-y,13,"collinearity: Collinearity among the constructs was examined using variance inflation factors (VIF), with values below 3.3 indicating no critical collinearity issues. (2)Assessment of path significance: The significance of the structural relationships was evaluated based on p-values, with p < 0.05 indicating statistically significant effects. (3)Assessment of explanatory power: The level of the coefficient of determination (R²) was assessed, with threshold values of 0.190 indicating weak, 0.333 indicating moderate, and 0.670 indicating substantial explanatory power. First, collinearity was assessed using the VIF. VIF values of 5 or higher indicate severe collinearity issues. In this study, all VIF values were within the acceptable threshold (VIF < 3.3). Therefore, no collinearity problems were detected in the structural model. Table 5. VIF MOV SE SDL TUGA MOV 2.695 SE 1.078 2.722 SDL TUGA 1.078 1 1.083 Second, the significance of the path coefficients was assessed using the bootstrapping procedure in SmartPLS. The t-values and p-values were used to determine whether the path coefficients (β) were statistically significant at the 5% significance level. A 5% significance level requires p < .050 and t > 1.96.",180
