DOC_060,s41598-026-54337-y_reference.pdf,10.1038/s41598-026-54337-y,14,"equivalently across male and female groups. Following the guidelines of Henseler, Ringle, et al. (2016) and Hair et al. (2022), the MICOM procedure involves three steps: configural invariance, compositional invariance, and the equality of composite means and variances. First, configural invariance was established because the same indicators, data treatment procedures, and algorithm settings were applied across the male and female groups. Second, compositional invariance was assessed using a permutation test. The correlations between the composite scores obtained from the original data and those from ACCEPTED MANUSCRIPT ARTICLE IN PRESS ARTICLE IN PRESS",92
