DOC_061,s41598-026-63076-z.pdf,10.1038/s41598-026-63076-z,8,"Scientific Reports | (2026) 16:33284 8 | https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-026-63076-z www.nature.com/scientificreports H8f. For further explanation, interaction graphs (using low and high SD values) were plotted (shown in Fig. 3), which shows that at higher levels of TAM and UTAT predictors, when hedonic motivation increases, it increases students’ behavioral intentions toward ChatGPT use. In contrast, at the lower level of TAM and UTAT predictors, when hedonic motivation decreases, it decreases students’ behavioral intentions toward ChatGPT use. This interaction implies that hedonic motivation strengthens the positive association between TAM and UTAT predictors and students’ behavioral intentions. Behavioral intentions also yielded a significant effect (ꞵ = 0.51, p = .02) on students’ attitudes toward using ChatGPT in their studies, with significant variance, i.e. R2 = 0.61, supporting, which supports hypothesis H9. Discussion The incorporation of AI has emerged as a critical factor in today’s educational system, significantly impacting how students learn. The effectiveness of employing AI in higher education is intricately linked to the attitudes and perceptions of students, as highlighted by Linardatos and Apostolou4. With the continuous emergence of new technologies like ChatGPT, it",180
DOC_061,s41598-026-63076-z.pdf,10.1038/s41598-026-63076-z,8,"system, significantly impacting how students learn. The effectiveness of employing AI in higher education is intricately linked to the attitudes and perceptions of students, as highlighted by Linardatos and Apostolou4. With the continuous emergence of new technologies like ChatGPT, it becomes crucial to delve into determinants that mold individuals’ perceptions toward its use. Therefore, this study offers practical verification to understand the dynamics of students’ attitudes and intentions toward ChatGPT usage employing the TAM and UTAT models as guiding frameworks. The results revealed high AU and BI among students who use ChatGPT. Coinciding with the prior studies, the use of an LLM-based platform has also been acknowledged as a frequently adopted application in earlier studies18,23. The adaptability of ChatGPT as a supporting means in learning was highlighted in a mixed-method study by Ngo6, which demonstrated its wide-ranging benefits, such as problem-solving and providing prompt feedback, among Vietnamese university students. Adeshola and Adepoju5 also signify ChatGPT as a virtual intelligent tutor that assists students, along with offering recommendations based on their prior outcomes, needs, and preferences. AU BI Mean SD T",180
