DOC_063,s42438-026-00697-7.pdf,10.1007/s42438-026-00697-7,10,"Postdigital Science and Education Table 1 (continued) Strobel category Original definition: technology affordances Operational definition: contextualize in HE Exemplary showcases Enabler Offers infrastructure for training, fine-tuning, or hosting GAI applications. Aims to make GAI easy to use without technical prior knowledge; spans all types without distinct boundaries in creativity or modification (e.g., Hugging Face, Writer, Cohere) Platforms and infrastructure that allow educators or institutions to build, customize, or deploy AI-powered learning tools — e.g., no-code platforms for creating subject-specific chatbots, LMS integrations that embed AI features into existing course environments, or fine-tuning platforms that let teachers adapt a base model to their curriculum 1. This study examines the use of ChatGPT to support critical thinking and argumentation skills in undergraduate international relations students. Compared to traditional debate, Chat- GPT-assisted sessions show greater improve- ment, suggesting potential value for integrating LLMs into education while noting contextual challenges (de la Puente et al. 2024) 2. This study examines ChatGPT’s impact on critical, creative, and reflective thinking in EFL learning. Results show greater gains in the ChatGPT group, with students noting both benefits",180
