NEW10,NEW10.pdf,10.1016/j.iheduc.2026.101105,7,"0.3 × SE) ÷ max session PRD × 100 (A.7) Progressive internalization; Metacognitive control; Self- regulated learning AI Response Utility Score (RU) Quality of AI integration Semantic Novelty (SN), Conceptual Transformation (CT), Contribution to Assignment (CF) RU = 0.45 × SN + 0.40 × CT + 0.15 × CF (A.8) Depth-of-processing; Constructive learning; Knowledge transformation; AI literacy AI-Driven Problem- Solving Score (PS) Depth of AI-supported reasoning Stepwise Alignment (SA), Conceptual Application (CA), Independent Expansion (IE) PS = 0.40 × SA + 0.40 × CA + 0.20 × IE (A.9) Scaffolding theory; Cognitive apprenticeship; Schema acquisition AI Response Complexity Score Perceived difficulty and usefulness Semantic Interpretation, Rephrasing Effort, Clarity Confidence, Usefulness, Cognitive Effort 10-item Likert-scale survey average (validated, α = 0.81) (A.10) Cognitive engagement; Cognitive effort; AI interpretability and trust Fig. 1. Study design and experimental flow showing participant enrollment, AI training workshops, stratified randomization, weekly task rotation, and data collection across 16 weeks. Distinct color bands denote the study phases: purple (setup and training), gray (experimental implementation), and blue (data collection and assessment). (For interpretation of the references to color",180
