NEW10,NEW10.pdf,10.1016/j.iheduc.2026.101105,8,"were timestamped and logged by session, course, and student ID, saved as TXT files, and automatically emailed to the study authors. 4. Randomization: Each student received eight AI and eight non-AI sessions across the semester, assigned weekly using a NumPy script that excluded absentees to maintain balance. The full Python script used for stratified randomization (randomization script), including seed control and week-by-week balancing logic, is openly available Fig. 2. Data aggregation and metric computation pipeline illustrating the sequential process from raw input files to final analytical dataset. The pipeline includes three phases: (1) Raw Inputs (yellow) - collection and cleaning of AI logs, assignments, and grades; (2) Data Integration (blue) - session-level matching and unified record construction; and (3) Metric Computation and Export (green) - metric calculation, dataset merging, and repository archiving. (For interpretation of the ref­ erences to color in this figure legend, the reader is referred to the web version of this article.) Table 2 Overview of analytical techniques. Analysis Purpose Dependent Variable (s) Predictors / Metrics and Analytical Level Parameters Output Reported Mann–Whitney U Compare performance between",180
